wsnorm's whitespace model is ASCII-only (space/tab/\n/\r): Unicode spaces
(NBSP U+00A0, ideographic space U+3000, …) are CONTENT, never collapsible
whitespace, so fillParts must never treat them as word-gap split points. This
pins that a NBSP-joined pair and a U+3000-joined pair each stay inside one
word cluster through a canonical re-wrap, byte-identical to the source.

-- input.gsx --
package p

component UnicodeSpaceContent() {
	<p>The trail sign says the summit sits 10 km ahead, but nobody mentioned that the last stretch climbs through loose gravel switchbacks before reaching a lookout named 日本　語 that the map never labels clearly at all.</p>
}
-- fmt.golden --
package p

component UnicodeSpaceContent() {
	<p>
		The trail sign says the summit sits 10 km ahead, but nobody mentioned that
		the last stretch climbs through loose gravel switchbacks before reaching a
		lookout named 日本　語 that the map never labels clearly at all.
	</p>
}
